  "name": "Stormbringer: Binder of Storms procs a Thunder Orb from Conduction (#3133)",
  "contract": "Binder of Storms (707542) promises \"Damage dealt by Conduction now has a 60% chance to summon a Thunder Orb\". Spell.dbc gives it Effect[0] SPELL_AURA_PROC_TRIGGER_SPELL with EffectTriggerSpell[0] 801802 and ProcChance 60, but ProcFlags 0 and an empty EffectSpellClassMask, so SpellMgr::LoadSpellProcs skips it and Aura::GetProcEffectMask never finds a proc entry: the aura is applied and never consulted again. Conduction (567560) is the only SpellFamilyName 22 spell with SpellFamilyFlags[0] 32768, so a proc entry with that family and mask selects it exactly. Twelve damaging Conduction hits at ProcChance 60 leave a false-failure probability of 0.4^12 = 1.7e-5 for the proc count. The untalented control casts the same Conduction at its own dummy, so a proc there would mean the orb comes from Conduction and not the talent.",
